# §7b witness (dirty.md §1.1: an own Structure field's working value is a reference, and its publication publishes the
# reference, never a copy of the referent): `Box: b` binds b's working reference, and `b\v` goes through it before
# anything is published -- first is 2.  The call publishes the reference; `b\v: 5` then writes the same Box, so the
# explicit `mytest\b\v` reads 5.  mytest gives 2 * 10 + 5 = 25; a publication that copies the Box gives 22.  (Rebinding
# one own Box field to another is refused today -- "graph assignment admission requires receiving-expression
# tests" -- so the stale-reference half of the model has no witness here.)
Box:
    int: v 0
end: Box

fn: nop () int
    return: 0
end: nop

fn: mytest () int
    b: merge: Box
    b\v: 2
    int: first 0
    first: b\v
    nop()
    b\v: 5
    int: seen 0
    seen: mytest\b\v
    return: first * 10 + seen
end: mytest

sendMessage: exit(exit_code: mytest(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
